#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""tg-archive: whole Telegram chats as local Markdown folders you (and an agent) can search and answer from. Python 3 stdlib.
Docs: CLAUDE.md "Telegram archive (tg-archive)". The download runs INSIDE the existing read-only Telegram MCP service (its
tool export_history, the same session, the same chat allowlist; nothing is ever sent); this script drives it through the MCP
gateway, takes the files from /srv/telegram-export and does everything else locally: whisper transcripts, video frame
candidates, OCR, PDF text and the Markdown.

  tg-archive chats [QUERY]                  chats the MCP may read (the allowlist): id, kind, title
  tg-archive run CHAT... [OPTIONS]          export + import + process + render, chat by chat (repeat = only what is new)
      --files KINDS   which files to download (default photo,video,video_note,voice; 'all' adds documents, audio, gif:
                      APKs, archives, PDFs); the others are listed as not downloaded, a later --files all fetches them
      --max-file-mb N skip files bigger than N MB (big videos are most of the time: Telegram gives about 5 MB/s per
                      account); a larger N later fetches the skipped ones
      --no-media      text only (no files; voice and video are then not transcribed); --files turns files on again
      --refresh       read the whole history again (edits, reactions); finished files are not downloaded again
      --lang L        whisper language (default auto; ru, uk, en, ...)
      --no-process    stop after the import (no whisper / OCR); render still runs
      --detach        run in the background as a transient user unit tg-archive-<id> (tg-archive status shows it)
      --verify        first check the archive's big files for zero-filled gaps and fetch the damaged ones again
      --folder NAME   keep the archive in $TG_ARCHIVE_ROOT/NAME/ (a folder of chats, with its own index.md); an archive
                      that is elsewhere is moved there
  tg-archive export CHAT [run's --files, --max-file-mb, --no-media, --refresh]   only the download and the import
  tg-archive process CHAT [--lang L] [--retry]      transcripts, frame candidates, OCR, document text (cached per message)
  tg-archive frames CHAT [--all] [--json]           videos whose frames are not chosen yet: transcript, candidates (time +
                                                    OCR), contact sheets, and the picks file to write
  tg-archive render CHAT|--all                      (re)build the Markdown from .raw/ (summary.md is never touched)
  tg-archive remote [status] | setup USER@HOST | all | long | off
                                                    a second whisper on another machine's NVIDIA GPU over ssh (key
                                                    login, uv there; no root): files from 2 min go there, the local
                                                    GPU keeps the short ones, both at once (long); all = every file
                                                    there, the local GPU only when it is down
  tg-archive links CHAT [--refresh] [--no-process]  what the messages link to (run does it beside the export): public
                                                    Notion pages with their sub-pages, databases and images (notion/),
                                                    YouTube videos up to 720p, transcribed with frames like a video
                                                    (transcripts/yt-<id>.md); then process and render
  tg-archive verify CHAT|--all                      find big files with zero-filled gaps (an interrupted pooled download),
                                                    remove them and what was made from them; the next run fetches them again
  tg-archive list | status [CHAT] | path CHAT

The choices of a chat (--no-media, --files, --max-file-mb, --lang) are kept in its .raw/settings.json: a later run (an
update) uses them, a flag given again changes them, and files the new choice wants (left out, too big, never queued) are
queued without reading the history again.
CHAT is a chat id (-100...), @username or t.me link, or (for chats already archived, and through `chats`) part of the title.
Archive: $TG_ARCHIVE_ROOT (default ~/Documents/tg-archive)/[FOLDER/]<title>-<id>/: index.md, messages/YYYY-MM.md (a forum
group: messages/<topic>/YYYY-MM.md, one folder per topic), transcripts/<id>.md, documents/<id>.md, media/, frames/,
summary.md (written by the agent), .raw/ (the source of everything else).
Frame picks: .raw/picks/<message id>.json = {"frames": [{"n": 3, "caption": "..."}]} ({"frames": []} = reviewed, none).
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 not available (the message says what to run), 4 the chat is not connected to the
MCP (the message lists the steps: join it in Telegram, mcp-telegram-setup chats, run again).
"""
